I1017 11:02:28.141936    7675 input_loop.go:106] HandleUserInput called with text: "The Worker has stopped in step 8 (reported the final analysis; step 8 has no approval stage). This run is condition F: there are no issue files. The Worker's latest chat reply is pasted below between the markers. You may also read the code and data in the Worker workspace (read-only). Then show your review (Part 1) and your draft to the Worker (Part 2) in full in your reply, in the format of Section 4 of MANAGER_BRIEF.md (in condition F, every draft is a chat message), and append \"Manager memo 09\" to memos/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/manager_memo.md as in Section 5. Append only: do not modify or delete any existing text in the memo file. Do not edit any other file.\n\n----- WORKER REPLY (pasted by the human) -----\n# Revised Triviality Search Report: Inhomogeneous Deformation of $C(n+1) = \\mathfrak{osp}(2|2n)$ (Issue I08-1)\n\n---\n\n### 1. Executive Summary & Revised Core Conclusion\n\nFollowing the identification of the **Koszul sign** governing the interaction between the odd central extension element $\\kappa$ ($p=1$) and the odd fermionic oscillator operators $a_1^\\sigma$ ($p=1$):\n$$a_1^\\sigma \\cdot \\kappa = (-1)^{p(a_1^\\sigma) p(\\kappa)} \\kappa \\cdot a_1^\\sigma = - \\kappa \\cdot a_1^\\sigma$$\nwe corrected the normal-ordering extraction of $\\kappa \\cdot \\gamma(X, Y)$ in `src/C_gamma.py`, re-generated Schema 2 and Schema 3, and re-computed the exact cohomology linear system for $C(2)$, $C(3)$, and $C(4)$.\n\n> **The Fundamental Theorem of $C(n+1)$ Inhomogeneous Deformation**:\n> For all $n \\ge 1$, the inhomogeneous deformation 2-cocycle $\\gamma(\\mathrm{gb})$ of $C(n+1) = \\mathfrak{osp}(2|2n)$ is **unconditionally a coboundary** for **all** deformation parameters $\\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s} \\in \\mathbb{C}$:\n> $$\\gamma(\\mathrm{gb}) \\in B^2(\\mathfrak{g}, \\mathfrak{g})_{\\bar{1}} \\quad \\text{for all } \\mathrm{gb} \\in \\mathbb{C}^{4n}.$$\n> Consequently, **the inhomogeneous deformation of $C(n+1) = \\mathfrak{osp}(2|2n)$ is unconditionally trivial for all values of $\\mathrm{gb}$**.\n> The obstruction space vanishes identically:\n> $$\\operatorname{Rank}([\\delta \\mid \\gamma]) - \\operatorname{Rank}(\\delta) = 0 \\quad (\\text{difference} = 0 \\text{ for all } n=1, 2, 3).$$\n\n---\n\n### 2. Case-Specific Evidence: Layer 3 vs. Layer 4 Comparison\n\nIn Layer 4, the test structure was generated by the reference involutive map $f_{\\text{ref}} = f_{\\text{mode\\_paired}}$ ([`data/C_1_coboundary.json`](file://<home>/notebook/git/thm01-R/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/data/C_1_coboundary.json)). Comparing this with the evaluated deformation $\\gamma|_{\\text{all\\_plus\\_one}}$ ([`data/C_1_evaluated.json`](file://<home>/notebook/git/thm01-R/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/data/C_1_evaluated.json)) provides concrete insight into the coboundary space:\n\n| Metric | $C(2)$ ($n=1$) | $C(3)$ ($n=2$) | $C(4)$ ($n=3$) |\n|---|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| Total Active Generator Pairs $(X, Y)$ | 58 | 321 | 974 |\n| Pairs in Evaluated Deformation $\\gamma$ | 54 | 292 | 876 |\n| Pairs in Reference Coboundary $\\delta f_{\\text{ref}}$ | 40 | 185 | 392 |\n| **Coinciding Pairs** (exact match between $\\gamma$ and $\\delta f_{\\text{ref}}$) | **4** | **12** | **24** |\n| **Differing Pairs** (active in both, different coefficients) | **32** | **156** | **344** |\n| **$\\gamma$-Only Pairs** (active in $\\gamma$, zero in $\\delta f_{\\text{ref}}$) | **18** | **124** | **508** |\n| **$\\delta f_{\\text{ref}}$-Only Pairs** (active in $\\delta f_{\\text{ref}}$, zero in $\\gamma$) | **4** | **25** | **92** |\n\n#### A. Coinciding Pairs\nFor specific root-mode channels, the evaluated deformation matches the test coboundary $\\delta f_{\\text{ref}}$ exactly:\n- $(E_{2\\delta_1}^+, E_{\\varepsilon+\\delta_1}) \\longmapsto +2 E_{2\\delta_1}^+$ in both $\\gamma$ and $\\delta f_{\\text{ref}}$.\n- $(E_{\\varepsilon+\\delta_1}, E_{2\\delta_1}^+) \\longmapsto -2 E_{2\\delta_1}^+$ in both $\\gamma$ and $\\delta f_{\\text{ref}}$.\n- $(E_{2\\delta_1}^-, E_{-\\varepsilon-\\delta_1}) \\longmapsto +2 E_{2\\delta_1}^-$ in both $\\gamma$ and $\\delta f_{\\text{ref}}$.\n- $(E_{-\\varepsilon-\\delta_1}, E_{2\\delta_1}^-) \\longmapsto -2 E_{2\\delta_1}^-$ in both $\\gamma$ and $\\delta f_{\\text{ref}}$.\n\n#### B. Differences Between the Test Map $\\delta f_{\\text{ref}}$ and $\\gamma$\nThe reference map $f_{\\text{ref}}$ chosen in Step 7 was a single isolated test map ($H_1 \\leftrightarrow E_{\\varepsilon+\\delta_1}$, $H_2 \\leftrightarrow E_{-\\varepsilon-\\delta_1}$). Naturally, $\\delta f_{\\text{ref}} \\ne \\gamma$ because $f_{\\text{ref}}$ is not the specific linear map that trivializes the `all_plus_one` profile.\n- For purely bosonic pairs $(E_{2\\delta_1}^+, E_{2\\delta_1}^-)$, $\\gamma = 0$ because $[b, b]$ is undeformed CCR, whereas $\\delta f_{\\text{ref}} = +4 E_{-\\varepsilon-\\delta_1} \\ne 0$ because $f_{\\text{ref}}(H_2) \\ne 0$.\n- However, as proven below, **there exists an exact odd linear map $f_{\\text{triv}} \\in \\operatorname{Hom}_{\\bar{1}}(\\mathfrak{g}, \\mathfrak{g})$ such that $\\gamma = \\delta f_{\\text{triv}}$ identically**.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Rigorous Analysis of the Koszul Sign & Cohomology\n\n#### 3.1 The Koszul Sign Mechanism\nIn the extended oscillator algebra, $\\kappa$ is an odd central generator ($p(\\kappa) = 1$).\nWhen evaluating brackets involving odd generators:\nFor $X = E_{\\varepsilon+\\delta_1} = a_1^+ b_1^+$:\n$$X^2 = a_1^+ (b_1^+ a_1^+) b_1^+ = a_1^+ (a_1^+ b_1^+ - \\mathrm{gb} \\cdot \\kappa) b_1^+ = - a_1^+ (\\mathrm{gb} \\cdot \\kappa) b_1^+.$$\nBecause $a_1^+$ has parity 1 and $\\kappa$ has parity 1:\n$$a_1^+ \\cdot \\kappa = - \\kappa \\cdot a_1^+.$$\nPulling $\\kappa$ to the left to match the standard schema expansion $[X, Y]_\\gamma = [X, Y]_0 + \\kappa \\cdot \\gamma(X, Y)$ yields:\n$$- a_1^+ (\\kappa \\cdot \\mathrm{gb}) b_1^+ = + \\kappa \\cdot \\mathrm{gb} \\cdot (a_1^+ b_1^+) \\implies \\gamma(X, X) = + 2 E_{\\varepsilon+\\delta_1}.$$\nWithout the Koszul sign $(-1)^{\\text{fermions to the left}}$, the odd-odd brackets incurred an erroneous relative sign flip of $-1$ relative to the even-odd brackets. This sign flip violated the super-Jacobi 2-cocycle identity $\\delta \\gamma = 0$, falsely creating an apparent non-zero cohomology class.\n\nWith the Koszul sign implemented in `src/C_gamma.py`, $\\gamma$ satisfies $\\delta \\gamma = 0$ identically.\n\n#### 3.2 Exact Rational Cohomology Ranks\nWe constructed the linear system $\\delta(\\phi) = \\gamma(\\mathrm{gb})$ over the entire space $\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\bar{1}}(\\mathfrak{g}, \\mathfrak{g})$ of odd linear maps $f(Z_j) = \\sum_i \\phi_{ij} Z_i$ using SymPy exact rational elimination:\n\n| Algebra | $\\dim \\mathfrak{g}$ | $\\dim \\operatorname{Hom}_{\\bar{1}}(\\mathfrak{g},\\mathfrak{g})$ | $\\mathrm{gb}$ Parameters | $\\operatorname{Rank}(\\delta) = \\dim B_{\\bar{1}}^2$ | $\\dim \\operatorname{Der}_{\\bar{1}}(\\mathfrak{g})$ | $\\operatorname{Rank}([\\delta \\mid \\gamma])$ | $\\operatorname{Rank}([\\delta \\mid \\gamma]) - \\operatorname{Rank}(\\delta)$ | Triviality Status |\n|---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| **$C(2)$** | $4 \\mid 4$ (8) | 32 | 4 | 28 | 4 | 28 | **0** | **TRIVIAL** |\n| **$C(3)$** | $11 \\mid 8$ (19) | 176 | 8 | 168 | 8 | 168 | **0** | **TRIVIAL** |\n| **$C(4)$** | $22 \\mid 12$ (34) | 528 | 12 | 516 | 12 | 516 | **0** | **TRIVIAL** |\n\n- In every case, $\\operatorname{Rank}([\\delta \\mid \\gamma]) = \\operatorname{Rank}(\\delta)$.\n- The difference is identically **0**.\n- **Every one of the $4n$ basis deformation cocycles is an exact coboundary**.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Explicit Form of the Trivializing Odd Linear Map $f$\n\nFor each deformation parameter $\\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s}$, the linear system yields an explicit odd linear map $f$ such that $\\gamma = \\delta f$.\n\nFor example, in $C(2)$ ($n=1$) under the representative Profile A (`all_plus_one` where all 4 parameters $= 1$), the exact trivializing map $f_{\\text{triv}}: \\mathfrak{g} \\to \\mathfrak{g}$ (with free gauge parameters set to 0) is given by:\n$$f(E_{\\varepsilon+\\delta_1}) = - H_2 - E_{2\\delta_1}^+$$\n$$f(E_{\\varepsilon-\\delta_1}) = + H_2 + E_{2\\delta_1}^-$$\n$$f(E_{-\\varepsilon+\\delta_1}) = - H_2 - E_{2\\delta_1}^+$$\n$$f(E_{-\\varepsilon-\\delta_1}) = + H_2 + E_{2\\delta_1}^-$$\n$$f(H_1) = E_{\\varepsilon+\\delta_1} - E_{\\varepsilon-\\delta_1} - E_{-\\varepsilon+\\delta_1} + E_{-\\varepsilon-\\delta_1}$$\n$$f(H_2) = 0, \\quad f(E_{2\\delta_1}^+) = 0, \\quad f(E_{2\\delta_1}^-) = 0.$$\n\nApplying the coboundary operator $\\delta$ to this explicit map reproduces the evaluated deformation $\\gamma|_{\\text{all\\_plus\\_one}}$ with **zero residual across all 64 generator pairs**:\n$$\\delta(f_{\\text{triv}}) = \\gamma|_{\\text{all\\_plus\\_one}}.$$\n\n---\n\n### 5. Final General Conjecture and Theorem\n\n> **Theorem (Triviality of $C(n+1)$ Inhomogeneous Deformation)**:\n> Let $\\mathfrak{g} = C(n+1) = \\mathfrak{osp}(2|2n)$ for any $n \\ge 1$.\n> Let $\\gamma(\\mathrm{gb})$ be the inhomogeneous deformation 2-cocycle defined on the abelian extension $L = \\mathfrak{g} \\oplus \\kappa \\mathfrak{g}$ by the exchange relations:\n> $$[b_j^s, a_1^\\sigma] = - \\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s} \\cdot \\kappa \\quad (\\sigma \\in \\{+,-\\},\\ j \\in \\{1,\\dots,n\\},\\ s \\in \\{+,-\\}).$$\n> \n> 1. **Universal Triviality**: For **all** parameter assignments $\\mathrm{gb} \\in \\mathbb{C}^{4n}$, the deformation cocycle $\\gamma(\\mathrm{gb})$ is a coboundary:\n>    $$\\gamma(\\mathrm{gb}) \\in B^2(\\mathfrak{g}, \\mathfrak{g})_{\\bar{1}}.$$\n> 2. **Vanishing Cohomology Class**: The induced cohomology class in the second adjoint Lie superalgebra cohomology vanishes identically:\n>    $$[\\gamma(\\mathrm{gb})] = 0 \\in H^2(\\mathfrak{g}, \\mathfrak{g})_{\\bar{1}} \\quad \\text{for all } \\mathrm{gb} \\in \\mathbb{C}^{4n}.$$\n> 3. **Algebra Isomorphism**: For all values of $\\mathrm{gb}$, the deformed Lie superalgebra $(\\mathfrak{g}, [\\cdot, \\cdot]_\\gamma)$ is isomorphic to the undeformed Lie superalgebra direct sum $(\\mathfrak{g}, [\\cdot, \\cdot]_0) \\oplus \\mathbb{C}\\kappa$ via the odd transformation:\n>    $$\\phi = \\operatorname{Id} + \\kappa \\cdot f_{\\mathrm{gb}}.$$\n\n---\n\n### 6. Summary of Completed Deliverables\n- **Koszul Sign Implementation**: Updated [`src/C_gamma.py`](file://<home>/notebook/git/thm01-R/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/src/C_gamma.py) to incorporate $(-1)^{\\text{fermions}}$ in `normal_order_word_ua`.\n- **Regenerated Datasets**:\n  - Layer 2: [`data/C_1_gamma.json`](file://<home>/notebook/git/thm01-R/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/data/C_1_gamma.json), [`data/C_2_gamma.json`](file://<home>/notebook/git/thm01-R/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/data/C_2_gamma.json), [`data/C_3_gamma.json`](file://<home>/notebook/git/thm01-R/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/data/C_3_gamma.json).\n  - Layer 3: [`data/C_1_evaluated.json`](file://<home>/notebook/git/thm01-R/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/data/C_1_evaluated.json), [`data/C_2_evaluated.json`](file://<home>/notebook/git/thm01-R/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/data/C_2_evaluated.json), [`data/C_3_evaluated.json`](file://<home>/notebook/git/thm01-R/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/data/C_3_evaluated.json).\n- **Automated Triviality Verification**: Created [`src/C_triviality_analysis.py`](file://<home>/notebook/git/thm01-R/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/src/C_triviality_analysis.py) and [`tests/test_C_triviality.py`](file://<home>/notebook/git/thm01-R/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/tests/test_C_triviality.py).\n- **Full Test Suite Status**: All 42 unit tests across the entire test suite pass.\n\nThis concludes the eight-step research investigation for $C(n+1) = \\mathfrak{osp}(2|2n)$.\n----- END OF WORKER REPLY -----"
